# Ocasio — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env
# For the local Supabase stack, use .env.local.example instead.
#
# `.env` and every other `.env.*` file are gitignored except the two templates.
# Never commit real credentials.
#
# Where each kind of variable lives:
#
#   Section 1  Frontend (VITE_*)   .env locally; Vercel → Project → Environment
#                                  Variables for Preview and Production
#   Section 2  Edge functions      `supabase secrets set` — never .env, never VITE_
#   Section 3  Database (Vault)    SQL against the hosted project — never a file
#   Section 4  Tests and CI        shell environment only; defaults suit the
#                                  local stack
#
# Development and production are separated by WHERE the values are set, not by
# extra files: development uses the local stack (.env.local.example), and
# Preview/Production values exist only in Vercel and Supabase.

# ===========================================================================
# 1. FRONTEND — PUBLIC
# ===========================================================================
#
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the client bundle at build time and
# is PUBLIC. `npm run build` FAILS if a required one is missing or invalid
# (vite.config.ts); the running app also refuses to start without them
# (src/lib/env.ts).

# REQUIRED. Supabase project URL — Project Settings > API > Project URL.
# Must be https:// in Preview and Production.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# REQUIRED. Supabase anon/public key — Project Settings > API > anon public.
#
# PUBLIC by design; it ships in the client bundle. It is only safe because Row
# Level Security is enabled on every table. Never put the service-role key here.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# OPTIONAL. The support inbox shown on the contact and legal pages
# (src/lib/site.ts). Leave unset until a real, monitored inbox exists: the
# pages then say the inbox is not configured instead of showing an address
# that receives no mail. The build prints a warning while it is unset.
VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# OPTIONAL. Which provider starts NEW payments:
#   test      (default) the deterministic local adapter. It cannot settle a
#             payment — only a signed webhook can — so it is safe everywhere.
#   razorpay  Razorpay Checkout. Needs the edge-function secrets in section 2
#             and the webhook configured, or payments cannot start or settle.
#             See docs/OCASIO_DEPLOYMENT.md §6.
# The Razorpay key id reaches the browser from payments-create-order, so there
# is no VITE_ variable for it — and the key secret never reaches the browser.
VITE_PAYMENT_PROVIDER=test

# ===========================================================================
# 2. EDGE FUNCTIONS — SERVER-ONLY (reference; do not set in this file)
# ===========================================================================
#
# Set on the hosted project with:
#   npx supabase secrets set RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=... RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=... RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...
# For local `supabase functions serve`, use supabase/functions/.env
# (template: supabase/functions/.env.example).
#
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_ID             rzp_test_… (sandbox) or rzp_live_… (production).
#                               Used by payments-create-order and payments-refund;
#                               the key id (not the secret) is returned to Checkout.
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET         server-only. Without it (or the key id) both
#                               functions refuse with 503.
#   RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET     the secret set on the Razorpay webhook.
#                               payments-webhook FAILS CLOSED without it.
#   RAZORPAY_API_BASE           development only — a stand-in for Razorpay's API.
#                               Leave unset in Preview and Production.
#   PAYMENT_PROVIDER            used only by payments-reconcile, which has no
#                               Razorpay adapter yet. Leave unset ("test").
#   RECONCILE_STALE_MINUTES     payments-reconcile threshold. Default 30.
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#                               injected by the platform.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   injected by the platform. Bypasses RLS. Must
#                               never reach the browser, this file, or any
#                               VITE_ variable.

# ===========================================================================
# 3. DATABASE VAULT — SERVER-ONLY (reference; do not set in this file)
# ===========================================================================
#
# The scheduled reconciliation sweep reads two Vault secrets and fails closed
# (writes a reconciliation.sweep_skipped audit row) until both exist:
#
#   ocasio_reconcile_url            https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/payments-reconcile
#   ocasio_reconcile_service_key    the project's service-role key
#
# See docs/OCASIO_OPERATIONS.md for the SQL.

# ===========================================================================
# 4. TESTS AND CI (reference; do not set in this file)
# ===========================================================================
#
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#       Override the local stack the Vitest and Playwright suites talk to.
#       Defaults are Supabase's published local-development keys.
#   SUPABASE_DB_URL
#       Direct Postgres connection for the tests that hold two transactions
#       open at once (concurrency). Default: the local stack, port 54322.
#   OCASIO_REQUIRE_SUPABASE=1
#       Make the integration suites FAIL instead of skipping when the stack is
#       unreachable. CI sets this.
#   CI
#       Set by GitHub Actions; Playwright then always starts a fresh server.
